    "body": "For example, the testcase in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1459671 would \"pass\" if you can target a frame if you're same origin-domain with its parent; that's the check in the fourth bullet of \"familiar with\".  So it could also be that the non-Firefox browsers do \"same origin\" in the first bullet and \"same origin-domain\" in the fourth bullet.  More tests needed to tell what they actually do.",
